(MUAC MEASUREMENT & ACUTE MALNUTRITION JOB AID) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Reference: TRN-NUTR-02 / Lesson 3 \(Downloadable Field Card\)) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(1. MUAC COLOUR CODE \(children 6-59 months\)) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   GREEN  >= 12.5 cm .... Normal nutrition status. Counsel the caregiver.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   YELLOW 11.5 - 12.4 cm . Moderate Acute Malnutrition \(MAM\).) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   RED    < 11.5 cm ...... Severe Acute Malnutrition \(SAM\). Refer today.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(2. MEASUREMENT STEPS) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   a. Use the LEFT arm; the arm must hang relaxed at the side.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   b. Find the mid-point between the shoulder tip and the elbow tip.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   c. Wrap the MUAC tape at the mid-point - snug, not tight.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   d. Read the window to the nearest 0.1 cm and record immediately.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(3. BILATERAL PITTING OEDEMA TEST) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   Press both feet with the thumbs for 3 seconds. If a pit remains in) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   BOTH feet, classify as SAM regardless of the MUAC reading.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(4. RUTF REFERRAL RULE) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   SAM without complications: OTP site, RUTF ration + routine medicines.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   SAM with complications \(no appetite, fever, oedema +++\): Stabilisation) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   Centre / hospital referral the same day.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
/F2 12 Tf
(5. WHAT THE CHV RECORDS IN CaafimaadHub) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   Children screened | MUAC readings | Oedema cases | Referrals issued.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(   Submit through 'Field Data Collection'. Works offline and auto-syncs.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
T*
